  "final_report": "## Structural Variant Investigation: chr2:96,300,000\n\n**BAM (as specified for this session):** `https://ftp-trace.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/ReferenceSamples/giab/data/AshkenazimTrio/HG002_NA24385_son/NIST_HiSeq_HG002_Homogeneity-10953946/NHGRI_Illumina300X_AJtrio_novoalign_bams/HG002.GRCh38.300x.bam`\n**Build (as specified):** GRCh38\n**Technology (as specified):** Illumina 300x paired-end, Novoalign aligner \u2014 this determines which evidence layers can apply (see `applicable_layers` result below, which independently confirmed data characteristics consistent with this).\n**Candidate breakpoint:** chr2:96,300,000\n\nAll findings below come only from `igv-breakpoint-assistant` MCP tool calls made in this session. Tool call order followed the MCP server's stated rules: `applicable_layers` \u2192 `bam_stats_at_locus` \u2192 `discordant_pairs` \u2192 `soft_clipped_reads` \u2192 `split_reads` \u2192 `read_depth_profile` \u2192 `breakpoint_evidence_summary`.\n\n### 1. Applicable evidence layers (`applicable_layers`)\nSampled 1000 reads from the BAM. Result: `applicable_layers = [\"discordant_pairs\", \"soft_clipped_reads\", \"read_depth\"]`. `split_reads` was found **not applicable** \u2014 \"no SA tags observed in 1000 sampled reads (consistent with an aligner that doesn't emit chimeric alignments),\" matching the stated Novoalign aligner.\n\n### 2. Locus quality check (`bam_stats_at_locus`, chr2:96,299,500\u201396,300,500)\n`total_reads=2346`, `mean_depth=302.74`, `mean_mapq=70`, `low_mapq_fraction=0`, `forward_reads=1212`, `reverse_reads=1134`. Low-MAPQ fraction of 0 is far below the tool's 0.4 repetitive-region caution threshold, so this is not a repetitive/low-confidence region \u2014 signals below can be read at face value. Depth (~303x) and roughly balanced strand counts are consistent with the stated 300x nominal coverage.\n\n### 3. Discordant pairs (`discordant_pairs`, chr2:96,300,000, \u00b1500bp)\n`total_reads_in_window=2323`, `discordant_pairs=5`, `discordant_fraction=0.002` (0.2%). Mates land on `{\"chr9\": 2, \"chr11\": 1, \"chr5\": 1, \"chr1\": 1}` \u2014 scattered across four different partner chromosomes, no more than 2 on any single one. Per the tool's own criterion (\"Real translocation = many discordant pairs clustering on ONE partner chromosome. Mates scattered across many different chromosomes = background noise\"), this pattern reads as background noise, not translocation signal.\n\n### 4. Soft-clipped reads (`soft_clipped_reads`, chr2:96,300,000, \u00b1200bp)\n`total_reads_in_window=1057`, `soft_clipped_reads=6`, `soft_clipped_fraction=0.006` (0.6%), `max_clips_at_position=1`, `dominant_clip_side=\"left\"` (`left_clip_reads=5`, `right_clip_reads=1`), consensus positions 96,299,688 (left) / 96,300,093 (right). The tool's own threshold states `max_clips_at_position < 3` = \"no real pileup, treat as noise\" \u2014 at 1, this is well below that, i.e., scattered clipping, not a breakpoint pileup.\n\n### 5. Split reads (`split_reads`, chr2:96,300,000, \u00b1200bp)\n`total_reads_in_window=1057`, `split_reads=0`, `split_read_fraction=0`, `partner_chromosomes={}`, `assessable=true` (reads were present in the window; zero of them were SA-tagged). This locus-level result is consistent with the whole-BAM `applicable_layers` finding that this aligner produced no SA tags anywhere.\n\n### 6. Read depth profile (`read_depth_profile`, chr2:96,297,000\u201396,303,000, 100bp bins, `focus_position=96300000`)\n`min_depth=215.24`, `max_depth=380.71`, `mean_depth=284.87`, `depth_ratio_min_to_mean=0.845`, `likely_deletion=false`. The region's true minimum (`dip_position=96,298,800`) is `dip_distance_from_focus=1200`bp from the candidate breakpoint, giving `dip_is_at_focus=false` (outside the tool's 1000bp default localization tolerance). So depth near 96,300,000 itself is unremarkable \u2014 the one real dip in the window belongs to a different, unrelated position.\n\n### 7. Composite summary (`breakpoint_evidence_summary`, passing `applicable_layers=[\"discordant_pairs\",\"soft_clipped_reads\",\"read_depth\"]`)\n- `evidence_score = 10` / 100 (normalized over the 3 applicable layers) \u2014 **primary finding per MCP server instructions**\n- `evidence_score_raw = 7.5` / 100 (over all 4 layers, unnormalized)\n- `evidence_strength = \"weak\"`, `signal_layers = \"1/3\"`\n- Component scores: `discordant_pair_score=7.5`, `soft_clip_score=0`, `split_read_score=0`, `depth_score=0`\n- `unassessable_layers = {}` (every applicable layer had reads to evaluate; nothing was skipped for lack of data)\n- Internally re-ran `read_depth_profile` at \u00b12000bp/200bp bins: `min_depth=219.28`, `max_depth=350.88`, `mean_depth=282.14`, `depth_ratio_min_to_mean=0.856`, same off-position dip at 96,298,800 (1200bp away, `dip_is_at_focus=false`) \u2014 corroborates step 6.\n- `supporting_observations`: \"5 discordant pair(s) (0% of reads in window) with mates mapping predominantly to chr9.\" and \"6 soft-clipped read(s) (1% of reads in window), consensus clip position at 96299688 (1 reads).\" \u2014 the depth dip is not listed as a supporting observation, consistent with `depth_score=0`.\n\n**Threshold provenance caveat (per the tool's own documentation, stated plainly as required):** of the 9 tier cutoffs behind these 4 component scores, only the read-depth layer's 0.7 moderate-tier threshold is empirically calibrated, and that only against a single confirmed real locus elsewhere. The other 8 thresholds (including the discordant-pair and soft-clip cutoffs applied above) are heuristic judgement calls not validated against real data beyond a handful of loci. `evidence_strength` is therefore an interpretable decomposition of what fired, not a calibrated probability.\n\n### Conclusion\nAcross all three layers this BAM can structurally produce signal for (discordant pairs, soft clips, read depth \u2014 `split_reads` is not applicable to this Novoalign-aligned data), the values at chr2:96,300,000 are consistent with normal high-coverage background noise rather than a structural variant:\n- Discordant pairs: 0.2% fraction, scattered across 4 chromosomes, no clustering on a single partner.\n- Soft clips: 0.6% fraction, max 1 read sharing any clip position (below the pileup threshold of 3).\n- Split reads: 0 (and the whole aligner produces no SA tags).\n- Depth: ratio 0.845\u20130.856 (above the 0.7 deletion threshold anyway), and the only real dip in the surrounding region is 1200bp away, not localized to this position.\n\nComposite `evidence_score = 10/100` (\"weak\"), with only 1 of 3 applicable layers contributing any nonzero score. **No credible evidence of a structural variant was found at chr2:96,300,000 in this session's tool outputs.**\n\nTwo conditional tools were deliberately **not** called, per their own stated trigger conditions: `gene_at_locus` (\"Call this after finding strong discordant/split-read evidence\" \u2014 not met here) and `reciprocal_breakpoint` (requires a clustering discordant-pair partner chromosome to verify \u2014 mates were scattered across 4 chromosomes with no dominant partner, so there was no candidate partner locus to check). `igv_screenshot`/`evidence_panel` were not generated as they fall outside the MCP server's required stats\u2192discordant\u2192soft_clips\u2192split_reads\u2192depth_profile\u2192summarize sequence and were not needed to answer the evidence question numerically.",
